#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:5
msgid "Content Security Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:13
msgid "What is Content Security Policy?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:15
msgid ""
"One of the best protections you have against XSS attacks is to implement "
"a Content Security Policy (CSP) on the site. This requires you to specify"
" and authorize each source of content that is included in your site's "
"HTML, including images, stylesheets, JavaScript files, and so on. The "
"browser will reject content from sources that are not explicitly "
"approved. This authorization is defined within the response's ``Content-"
"Security-Policy`` header and offers various configuration options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:23
msgid ""
"This sounds complex, and on some sites, can definitely be challenging. "
"For many simple sites, though, where all content is served by the same "
"domain (e.g., **http://example.com**), it is very simple to integrate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:26
msgid ""
"As this is a complex subject, this user guide will not go over all of the"
" details. For more information, you should visit the following sites:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:29
msgid ""
"`Content Security Policy main site <https://content-security-"
"policy.com/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:30
msgid "`W3C Specification <https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/outgoing/csp.rst:31
